From ba2f8fa1fdf4c4bfbefd90cc30667fc7542828f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:39:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat links: tighten the profile-board ledger
 fallback (PR #2372 review nits)

Review 5894115299 of PR #2372 (card t_01a1d59ed82faeb0) flagged four
behaviours of the profile-board ledger fallback in replica_cards/links_diff:

1. links_diff trusted every qualified non-default-owner row missing from a
   readable replica as a profile-own-board card, so a shared-board card of a
   `work` owner lost in sync read clean while the same `default` row read
   unclean. links_diff now returns `profile_board` (ids per chat, shaped like
   only_in_ledger; `hermes kanban sync links-diff` prints it), and an
   every-chat read marks `owner_on_board` when the replica carries another
   ledger card of the same owner gateway+profile on that board: that profile
   syncs through the shared board, so links_diff reports its missing card as
   only_in_ledger instead of trusting it. The reader still lists it (union).
2. replica_cards read the ledger (waiting on a projection rebuild) on every
   call, even with no replica rows. With no rows and a last projection
   holding no profile-board card it now takes that projection stale_ok
   (background rebuild), so the call no longer queues.
3. The carry probe ran over every chat's profile-board cards; the lineage
   filter now applies before it (the owner-evidence probe runs only for
   every-chat reads).
4. A closed-card reader got a released replica link as an explicit released
   row but no released profile-board card; both are released rows now
   (status, released, unfinished=False, release_reason=link_released).

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_chat_links_profile_board.py, 5 tests:
all 5 fail on the base hermes_cli/ (1-4 on the behaviour, the unreadable
probe guard on the missing helper) and pass here. 32 files importing
kanban_chat_links / links_diff / replica_cards: 649 passed.
